From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:04:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] acpi: Optionally skip the SLIC lookup in CBFS

write_acpi_tables() looks for the CBFS file slic on every boot, and
cbfs_map() warns "CBFS: 'fallback/slic' not found." when the image has
none. On a board whose images never carry that file, it is a warning
on every boot for a file that is not meant to be there.

Add ACPI_SLIC_CBFS, default y as before. With N, coreboot does not
look for the file. The MSDM table from a product key in the VPD does
not depend on it.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x with ACPI_SLIC_CBFS=n: no CBFS warning for
slic in the ramstage log, and the MSDM table built from the VPD is
still among the ACPI tables.

Change-Id: I876f41a8356594a39fb7135da15023c80dbede13
---
 src/acpi/Kconfig | 10 ++++++++++
 src/acpi/acpi.c  |  4 +++-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/acpi/Kconfig b/src/acpi/Kconfig
index ef1dde89fcb..884f128d2d7 100644
--- a/src/acpi/Kconfig
+++ b/src/acpi/Kconfig
@@ -100,6 +100,16 @@ config ACPI_LPIT
 	help
 	  Selected by platforms that support and fill Intel Low Power Idle Table.
 
+config ACPI_SLIC_CBFS
+	bool "Add a SLIC or MSDM table from the CBFS file slic"
+	depends on HAVE_ACPI_TABLES
+	default y
+	help
+	  Look for the CBFS file slic and add the SLIC or MSDM table it holds.
+	  Say N on a board whose images never carry that file: coreboot then
+	  does not look for it, and does not warn on every boot that it is
+	  missing. A product key in the VPD still gives the MSDM table.
+
 menu "Windows SMM Security Mitigations Table"
 	depends on HAVE_ACPI_TABLES && HAVE_SMI_HANDLER
 
diff --git a/src/acpi/acpi.c b/src/acpi/acpi.c
index 6dd578a063a..d10a1963c9f 100644
--- a/src/acpi/acpi.c
+++ b/src/acpi/acpi.c
@@ -1751,7 +1751,9 @@ static unsigned long write_acpi_tables(const unsigned long start)
 		return start;
 	}
 
-	slic_file = cbfs_map(CONFIG_CBFS_PREFIX "/slic", &slic_size);
+	slic_file = NULL;
+	if (CONFIG(ACPI_SLIC_CBFS))
+		slic_file = cbfs_map(CONFIG_CBFS_PREFIX "/slic", &slic_size);
 	if (slic_file
 	    && (slic_file->length > slic_size
 		|| slic_file->length < sizeof(acpi_header_t)
